---
import '../styles/global.css'
import '../styles/landing.css'

const PATHWAY = [
  ['01', 'From slopes to learning', 'calculus'],
  ['02', 'Numbers with direction', 'vectors'],
  ['03', 'Following cause and effect', 'computation graphs'],
  ['04', 'Learning from mistakes', 'backpropagation'],
  ['05', 'Getting better step by step', 'optimization'],
  ['06', 'Choosing among possibilities', 'probability'],
  ['07', 'Turning words into meaning', 'tokens and embeddings'],
  ['08', 'Deciding what matters', 'attention'],
  ['09', 'Building a transformer', 'transformer blocks'],
  ['10', 'Teach your own tiny model', 'training lab'],
]
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Crect width='32' height='32' fill='%2320221f'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='16' cy='16' r='6' fill='%23c85d31'/%3E%3C/svg%3E" />
    <meta name="description" content="Begin with calculus. End with a transformer that you trained. Mathos turns every answer into a better path forward." />
    <title>Mathos — From calculus to your own tiny transformer</title>
  </head>
  <body class="landing-page" data-story="1">
    <a class="skip-link" href="#story">Skip to the story</a>
    <header class="landing-header">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Mathos home">MATHOS<span>·</span></a>
      <p>Calculus <span>→</span> transformer</p>
      <a class="header-cta" href="/learn">Enter the studio <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <aside class="path-motif" aria-hidden="true">
      <p><span>01</span> Learning path <b>10</b></p>
      <svg viewBox="0 0 180 610" role="presentation">
        <path class="motif-base" d="M90 18 C90 66 36 72 36 126 C36 180 144 176 144 234 C144 292 63 298 63 354 C63 416 132 414 132 470 C132 524 90 530 90 590" />
        <path class="motif-progress" pathLength="1" d="M90 18 C90 66 36 72 36 126 C36 180 144 176 144 234 C144 292 63 298 63 354 C63 416 132 414 132 470 C132 524 90 530 90 590" />
        <g class="motif-nodes">
          <circle cx="90" cy="18" r="5" />
          <circle cx="36" cy="126" r="5" />
          <circle cx="144" cy="234" r="5" />
          <circle cx="63" cy="354" r="5" />
          <circle cx="132" cy="470" r="5" />
          <circle cx="90" cy="590" r="7" />
        </g>
      </svg>
      <div class="motif-state"><span>Now</span><strong>Slopes</strong></div>
      <div class="motif-state end"><span>Then</span><strong>Your model</strong></div>
    </aside>

    <main id="story">
      <section class="story-section hero-section is-visible" data-story-step="1">
        <div class="section-inner hero-inner">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span>Mathos learning system</span><span>Chapter 01 / 05</span></p>
          <div class="company-proof" aria-label="Mathos company proof">
            <span>Backed by <strong>Y Combinator</strong></span>
            <span>Featured in <strong>Forbes</strong></span>
            <span>Built for <strong>5M+ learners</strong></span>
          </div>
          <h1>Begin with<br /><em>calculus.</em><br />End with a transformer<br />that <i>you trained.</i></h1>
          <div class="hero-bottom">
            <p>One connected path from the mathematics you can see to the intelligence you can build.</p>
            <a class="primary-link" href="/learn">Start with calculus <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="scroll-cue">Scroll to follow the calculation <span>↓</span></p>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section evidence-section" data-story-step="2">
        <div class="section-inner evidence-layout">
          <div class="section-index"><span>02</span><p>One answer changes the path</p></div>
          <div class="answer-evidence" aria-label="An answer of 36 becomes evidence for a missed path">
            <p class="answer-number">36</p>
            <p class="answer-label">Not just wrong.<br /><strong>Specific.</strong></p>
          </div>
          <div class="evidence-copy">
            <p class="lead">36 tells Mathos you followed the product path—and missed the direct one.</p>
            <div class="decision-line">
              <span>Answer</span><b>→</b><span>Evidence</span><b>→</b><span>New path</span>
            </div>
            <p>So the lesson changes. The representation changes. Then a fresh problem checks whether the idea can travel.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section representation-section" data-story-step="3">
        <div class="section-inner">
          <div class="section-index light"><span>03</span><p>The same idea changes representation</p></div>
          <h2>Follow the path.<br /><em>Change the lens.</em></h2>
          <div class="representation-sequence">
            <article>
              <span class="rep-number">01</span>
              <div><strong>dy/dx</strong><i> = 40</i></div>
              <p>Equation</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="rep-number">02</span>
              <div class="branch-mark"><i></i><i></i><b></b><i></i></div>
              <p>Computation graph</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="rep-number">03</span>
              <div class="vector-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
              <p>Vectors + attention</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="rep-number">04</span>
              <div class="transformer-mark"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
              <p>Transformer</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <p class="representation-note">The notation gets more powerful. The underlying habit stays the same: trace influence, combine evidence, update what happens next.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section pathway-section" data-story-step="4">
        <div class="section-inner pathway-layout">
          <div class="pathway-intro">
            <div class="section-index"><span>04</span><p>Ten stages. One climb.</p></div>
            <h2>From a slope<br />to a system<br /><em>that learns.</em></h2>
            <p>Mathos already lives where mathematical reasoning happens. That makes it the right place to connect explanation, evidence, practice, and a real model you can inspect.</p>
            <strong>Built by Mathos.</strong>
          </div>
          <ol class="landing-pathway">
            {PATHWAY.map(([number, label, meta]) => (
              <li>
                <span>{number}</span>
                <div><strong>{label}</strong><small>{meta}</small></div>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="story-section finale-section" data-story-step="5">
        <div class="section-inner finale-inner">
          <div class="section-index light"><span>05</span><p>The final challenge</p></div>
          <p class="finale-kicker">A real learning system, not a course playlist.</p>
          <h2>Teach a tiny<br />transformer to<br /><em>finish the pattern.</em></h2>
          <div class="finale-bottom">
            <p>First, show us how you think about a derivative. Mathos will take it from there.</p>
            <a class="primary-link light-link" href="/learn">Start with calculus <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <footer><span>MATHOS·</span><span>Built for the path between knowing and building.</span></footer>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script is:inline>
      const REDUCED_MOTION = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches
      const STORY_SECTIONS = [...document.querySelectorAll('[data-story-step]')]

      if (REDUCED_MOTION) {
        STORY_SECTIONS.forEach((section) => section.classList.add('is-visible'))
        document.body.dataset.story = '5'
      } else {
        document.body.classList.add('motion-ready')
        const reveal_observer = new IntersectionObserver((entries) => {
          entries.forEach((entry) => {
            if (!entry.isIntersecting) return
            entry.target.classList.add('is-visible')
            document.body.dataset.story = entry.target.dataset.storyStep
          })
        }, { rootMargin: '-20% 0px -45%', threshold: 0.08 })

        STORY_SECTIONS.forEach((section) => reveal_observer.observe(section))
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
